## 解答

**S1 — Recall the $myb72^{-/-}$ baseline (sub_prev).**

From the prior step, in the $myb72^{-/-}$ single mutant under phosphate deficiency:
- Severed arrow: $MYB72 \xrightarrow{\text{enzymatic\_induction}} F6'H1$
- Unreachable nodes: $\{F6'H1, Coumarins, \Delta Microbiota\}$
- Preserved upstream activity: $PHR1 \xrightarrow{\text{transcriptional\_activation}} MYB72^{\varnothing}$ (PHR1 is active but signal cannot propagate past $MYB72^{\varnothing}$)
- $\Delta Microbiota$ is absent; MYB72 is necessary for the downstream sub-chain.

**S2 — Apply the $phr1$ lesion on top of the $myb72$ lesion (double mutant).**

In the $myb72^{-/-}$ single mutant, the arrow $PHR1 \xrightarrow{\text{transcriptional\_activation}} MYB72$ was structurally intact (PHR1 was active and did signal toward $MYB72$), even though $MYB72$ was non-functional. In the double mutant $phr1^{-/-}\,myb72^{-/-}$, PHR1 itself is completely non-functional, severing that first arrow at its source.

**(i) ADDITIONAL_SEVERED_ARROW:**
The $phr1$ lesion severs $PHR1 \xrightarrow{\text{transcriptional\_activation}} MYB72$. This arrow was present (though producing only $MYB72^{\varnothing}$) in the $myb72^{-/-}$ single-mutant baseline; it is now severed at the source in the double mutant. This is the one additional severed arrow relative to the $myb72^{-/-}$ baseline.

**(ii) UNREACHABLE_NODES:**
With PHR1 non-functional, no signal enters the chain at any node. Every node downstream of PHR1 — i.e., $\{MYB72, F6'H1, Coumarins, \Delta Microbiota\}$ — is unreachable. (In the $myb72^{-/-}$ single mutant, MYB72 was nominally reached as a target but produced no output; in the double mutant, MYB72 is also unreachable as a target of PHR1.)

**(iii) PRESERVED_UPSTREAM_ACTIVITY:**
None. PHR1 itself is non-functional. There is no active node in the chain; no upstream signaling activity is preserved.

**(iv) EPISTASIS_CLASSIFICATION:**
Compare the double mutant to each single mutant with respect to $\Delta Microbiota$:
- **vs. $myb72^{-/-}$:** $\Delta Microbiota$ is absent in both. Adding the $phr1$ lesion to $myb72^{-/-}$ produces no additional change in $\Delta Microbiota$. The $myb72$ lesion already fully occludes the downstream phenotype; the $phr1$ lesion is redundant with respect to $\Delta Microbiota$. This is linear occlusion epistasis.
- **vs. $phr1^{-/-}$:** $\Delta Microbiota$ is absent in both (the $phr1^{-/-}$ single mutant cannot activate MYB72, so the chain is already broken at the first arrow). Adding the $myb72$ lesion to $phr1^{-/-}$ likewise produces no additional change in $\Delta Microbiota$.
- **Epistasis direction:** PHR1 is upstream of MYB72 in the strictly linear chain. The $phr1$ lesion is epistatically upstream; the $myb72$ lesion is epistatically downstream. Because both single mutants already abolish $\Delta Microbiota$, the double mutant is phenotypically equivalent to either single mutant — a classic linear-pathway occlusion epistasis pattern.

**(v) LOGICAL_CONCLUSION:**
$\text{NECESSARY}(PHR1)$ for transcriptional activation of MYB72; $\text{NECESSARY}(MYB72)$ for enzymatic induction of F6'H1 and the downstream sub-chain $\{F6'H1 \xrightarrow{\text{biosynthesis}} Coumarins \xrightarrow{\text{rhizosphere\_secretion}} \Delta Microbiota\}$. In $phr1^{-/-}\,myb72^{-/-}$, $\Delta Microbiota \equiv$ absent, indistinguishable from either single mutant; no new pathway is unmasked; strict linear epistasis is confirmed with PHR1 upstream of MYB72, and the double-mutant result is fully consistent with the fixed strictly linear topology.

最终答案：\boxed{
\text{ADDITIONAL\_SEVERED\_ARROW: } PHR1 \xrightarrow{\text{transcriptional\_activation}} MYB72 \text{ (severed by } phr1^{-/-} \text{; this arrow was intact in } myb72^{-/-} \text{ baseline, beyond the } MYB72 \xrightarrow{\text{enzymatic\_induction}} F6'H1 \text{ arrow already severed in } myb72^{-/-}\text{)}
\;\Big|\;
\text{UNREACHABLE\_NODES: } \{MYB72,\; F6'H1,\; Coumarins,\; \Delta Microbiota\}
\;\Big|\;
\text{PRESERVED\_UPSTREAM\_ACTIVITY: } \varnothing \text{ (PHR1 non-functional; no active node in chain)}
\;\Big|\;
\text{EPISTASIS\_CLASSIFICATION: } \Delta Microbiota_{phr1^{-/-}myb72^{-/-}} \equiv \Delta Microbiota_{myb72^{-/-}} \equiv \Delta Microbiota_{phr1^{-/-}} \equiv \text{absent}\text{; linear occlusion epistasis; } PHR1 \text{ is epistatically UPSTREAM of } MYB72\text{; adding } phr1 \text{ lesion to } myb72^{-/-} \text{ produces no additional change in } \Delta Microbiota\text{; double-mutant unmasks no additional pathway}
\;\Big|\;
\text{LOGICAL\_CONCLUSION: } \text{NECESSARY}(PHR1) \text{ for } PHR1 \xrightarrow{\text{transcriptional\_activation}} MYB72\text{; } \text{NECESSARY}(MYB72) \text{ for } \{F6'H1 \xrightarrow{\text{biosynthesis}} Coumarins \xrightarrow{\text{rhizosphere\_secretion}} \Delta Microbiota\}\text{; } phr1^{-/-}myb72^{-/-} \text{ confirms strict linear necessity of both nodes with } PHR1 \text{ upstream and } MYB72 \text{ downstream; no bypass; double-mutant } \Delta Microbiota \equiv \text{absent, indistinguishable from either single mutant}
}

## 解答

S1 — Recall prior result (sub_prev): The strictly linear chain PHR1 →^{transcriptional_activation} MYB72 →^{enzymatic_induction} F6'H1 →^{biosynthesis} Coumarins →^{rhizosphere_secretion} ΔMicrobiota was established under phosphate deficiency. Both PHR1 and MYB72 are individually necessary; the double mutant phr1^{-/-} myb72^{-/-} yields ΔMicrobiota ≡ absent, confirming linear occlusion epistasis with PHR1 epistatically upstream of MYB72. No bypass path exists within the fixed node set.

S2 — Key topological constraint: Because the chain is strictly linear and PHR1^{GOF} can only act through the arrow PHR1 →^{transcriptional_activation} MYB72, any downstream severed arrow remains severed regardless of PHR1 activity level.

S3 — Background (A): PHR1^{GOF} in myb72^{-/-}:
  • PHR1^{GOF} fires the arrow PHR1 →^{transcriptional_activation} MYB72 constitutively.
  • However, MYB72 protein is completely absent (myb72^{-/-}); therefore the arrow MYB72 →^{enzymatic_induction} F6'H1 is severed.
  • By strict linear propagation, F6'H1, Coumarins, and ΔMicrobiota are all unreachable.
  • Classification: PHR1^{GOF} is INSUFFICIENT; ΔMicrobiota ≡ absent; No-Rescue.
  • Residual severed arrow: MYB72 →^{enzymatic_induction} F6'H1.

S4 — Background (B): PHR1^{GOF} in phr1^{-/-}:
  • Endogenous PHR1 is absent, but PHR1^{GOF} supplies constitutive, complete PHR1 transcriptional activation activity, fully replacing the absent endogenous locus.
  • Arrow PHR1^{GOF} →^{transcriptional_activation} MYB72 is now active.
  • MYB72 is wild-type functional; arrow MYB72 →^{enzymatic_induction} F6'H1 is intact.
  • Full chain propagates: F6'H1 →^{biosynthesis} Coumarins →^{rhizosphere_secretion} ΔMicrobiota.
  • Classification: PHR1^{GOF} is SUFFICIENT; ΔMicrobiota ≡ present; Rescue.
  • Residual severed arrow: ∅.

S5 — Background (C): PHR1^{GOF} in wild-type:
  • All five nodes are functional; PHR1^{GOF} adds constitutive activity on an already-intact chain.
  • Full chain propagates trivially.
  • Classification: PHR1^{GOF} is SUFFICIENT (trivially); ΔMicrobiota ≡ present; Rescue.
  • Residual severed arrow: ∅.

S6 — Unifying sufficiency predicate: Comparing (A) No-Rescue vs. (B) and (C) Rescue, the distinguishing condition is the functional status of MYB72. In (A), MYB72 is non-functional (null); in (B) and (C), MYB72 is functional. Therefore:
  SUFFICIENT(PHR1^{GOF} → ΔMicrobiota | background) ⟺ MYB72 is functional in that background.

S7 — Logical conclusion: In a strictly linear chain, gain-of-function at PHR1 can only restore the arrow PHR1 →^{transcriptional_activation} MYB72. It cannot circumvent a downstream lesion at MYB72 because MYB72 is the obligate downstream transducer; no bypass path exists within {PHR1, MYB72, F6'H1, Coumarins, ΔMicrobiota}. PHR1^{GOF} rescues ΔMicrobiota if and only if MYB72 is present and functional.

最终答案：\boxed{
  BACKGROUND_OUTCOMES:
    (A) PHR1^{GOF} in myb72^{-/-}: INSUFFICIENT → ΔMicrobiota ≡ absent; No-Rescue;
    (B) PHR1^{GOF} in phr1^{-/-}: SUFFICIENT → ΔMicrobiota ≡ present; Rescue;
    (C) PHR1^{GOF} in wild-type: SUFFICIENT → ΔMicrobiota ≡ present; Rescue;

  RESIDUAL_SEVERED_ARROW:
    (A) MYB72 →^{enzymatic_induction} F6'H1  [persists despite PHR1^{GOF}];
    (B) ∅  [no arrow severed; full chain intact];
    (C) ∅  [no arrow severed; full chain intact];

  UNIFYING_SUFFICIENCY_PREDICATE:
    SUFFICIENT(PHR1^{GOF} → ΔMicrobiota | background) ⟺ MYB72 is functional in that background;
    equivalently: PHR1^{GOF} is INSUFFICIENT to rescue ΔMicrobiota in any background where MYB72 is non-functional (null);

  LOGICAL_CONCLUSION:
    NECESSARY(MYB72) for PHR1^{GOF} →^{transcriptional_activation} MYB72 →^{enzymatic_induction} F6'H1 →^{biosynthesis} Coumarins →^{rhizosphere_secretion} ΔMicrobiota;
    PHR1^{GOF} is INSUFFICIENT to rescue ΔMicrobiota in myb72^{-/-} because MYB72 is the obligate downstream transducer;
    PHR1^{GOF} is SUFFICIENT to rescue ΔMicrobiota in phr1^{-/-} because MYB72 is functional and the chain is otherwise intact;
    no bypass path exists within {PHR1, MYB72, F6'H1, Coumarins, ΔMicrobiota};
    gain-of-function at PHR1 cannot circumvent a downstream lesion at MYB72 in a strictly linear chain.
}

